76-bd19-11fe65ed6396" :question/math-academy-id "q-282146" :question/problem "Let $a=2i-7j+4k$ and $b=5i+3j-6k.$ Find $a\\times b.$\n\n$a\\times b=$\n\n{{field-1}}$\\,i\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,j\\,+\\,$\n{{field-3}}$\\,k$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -7 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -7 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =((-7)(-6)-(4)(3))i-((2)(-6)-(4)(5))j+((2)(3)-(-7)(5))k \\\\  & =(42-12)i-(-12-20)j+(6+35)k \\\\  & =30\\,i+32\\,j+41\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295231 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a64fae9d-e2e5-5cc2-97a3-c76e01024a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a64fae9d-e2e5-5cc2-97a3-c76e01024a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293588} :answer-field/id #uuid "6614727d-b3f9-5cfe-8f00-ff4fd92922c0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294286} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38e04374-186e-531f-9bbd-204857144c91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38e04374-186e-531f-9bbd-204857144c91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293168} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fb00d26-4755-51aa-a0f6-c647ce7f15c8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294379} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b24ae11-d3ff-5757-ae83-2080ccdf501b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b24ae11-d3ff-5757-ae83-2080ccdf501b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293174} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b6ee88b-a46d-51b5-b533-fb989c656058" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294426}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3fcf3e73-8775-529c-878e-bbc1947caeb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-282147" :question/problem "Let $a=-4i+3k$ and $b=i+2j-2k.$ Find $a\\times b.$\n\n$a\\times b=$\n\n{{field-1}}$\\,i\\,-\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,j\\,-\\,$\n{{field-3}}$\\,k$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}-4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}-4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(0)(-2)-(3)(2)i-(-4)(-2)-(3)(1)j+(-4)(2)-(0)(1)k \\\\  & =(0-6)i-(8-3)j+(-8-0)k \\\\  & =-6\\,i-5\\,j-8\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295235 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6399e3b8-ff34-55fc-a47f-71dc471f219c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6399e3b8-ff34-55fc-a47f-71dc471f219c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293339} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fd515cd-c214-5167-b7ba-c4def2042247" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294272} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d675942-4fa7-5d27-8386-58830bed7ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d675942-4fa7-5d27-8386-58830bed7ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293390} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3f82250-dec1-5957-8cd9-d5e3812caae9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294676}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a3a69df9-3422-55c4-b6e2-d44c3f81e8dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-282260" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2x,3,1⟩,$ $b=⟨-2x,0,4⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{280}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 3 & 1 \\\\ -2x & 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}2x & 1 \\\\ -2x & 4\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}2x & 3 \\\\ -2x & 0\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(12-0)i-(8x+2x)j+(0+6x)k \\\\  & =⟨12,-10x,6x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{12}^{2}+(-10x)^{2}+(6x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+100{x}^{2}+36{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{136{x}^{2}+144}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{280} \\\\ \\sqrt{136{x}^{2}+144} & =\\sqrt{280} \\\\ 136{x}^{2}+144 & =280 \\\\ 136{x}^{2} & =136 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-1,$ $x=1.$"}]}
